  "cutoff 2026-08-18T00:00Z on all analyses, strictly exclusive; the pull ran 4.5 h after it, so no in-scope day is partial. 08-17 cells are labelled provisional as standing discipline.",
  "THREE-DAY WINDOW: issues #4->#5 lapsed while the lemmy.world comparator was re-crawled. Window-only cells cover 3 calendar days against issue #4's 1 and are NOT window-vs-window comparable to it. The window starts at issue #4's last captured item (08-15 05:10), so 08-15 is partial INSIDE the window.",
  "newcomer window m=221, ABOVE the standing m>=100 floor: the matched NN cell, within-pool parity and union cells are all computed and none is supplementary this issue.",
  "delta pipeline: claims and allocation labels cached by kind:id; 2,525 items claimified and 2,572 classified this issue; 0 cache evictions for edits (0 edited items found across 9,519 compared).",
  "single-normalizer / bge-only: rolling series, newcomer and refresh cells are Qwen-normalized and bge-embedded; the three-embedder check covers placement only.",
  "allocation LEVEL carries the parent study's 0.31-0.71 specification range; kappa(Qwen,Gemma)=0.4278 on the agent pool. The TREND is the cleaner object.",
  "the lemmy.world reference is FROZEN (2023-06 founding month, 55,223 items) and read from results/lemmy_baseline/results.json; it is never re-measured per issue. Its platform share is 0.4665 [0.4515, 0.4853] author-clustered - a point estimate with a band, not a sharp threshold.",
  "the lemmy frame is 55.7% meta-tier with c/lemmyworld alone 41.7%, a property of the pre-arrival cohort that over-weights meta and makes the human benchmark MORE self-referential; direction known, magnitude not (baseline s2).",
  "fixed-horizon permeability and the fixed-span churn control both average over cohort sets whose MEMBERSHIP grows each issue; they remove the opportunity confound, not the membership one.",
  "core_n is retired as a series: the published climb has no counterpart under the fixed-span control.",
